  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has a **strictly increasing** sequence AAA of length NNN that he wants to convert into an arithmetic progression†^{\\dagger}†.\n\nIn one operation, Chef can choose some integer, and then insert it anywhere into the array.\n\nFind the minimum operations required for Chef to achieve his goal. It can be proven that it is possible under the constraints of this problem.\n\n†^{\\dagger}† A sequence AAA of length NNN is called an Arithmetic progression if Ai−Ai−1A_i - A_{i - 1}Ai​−Ai−1​ is constant for all 1≤i&lt;N1 \\le i &lt; N1≤i&lt;N. For example, [1,3,5,7,9][1, 3, 5, 7, 9][1,3,5,7,9] and [3][3][3] are arithmetic progressions but not [1,5,7,9][1, 5, 7, 9][1,5,7,9].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum operations needed for Chef.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤1002 \\le N \\le 1002≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "Ai&lt;Ai+1A_i \\lt A_{i + 1}Ai​&lt;Ai+1​"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 3\n3\n1 7 9\n4\n1 42 43 100",
        "output": "0\n2\n96",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The given sequence is already an Arithmetic progression.\nTest Case 2 : Chef adds the integers 333 and 555 between 111 and 777 to get the sequence [1,3,5,7,9][1, 3, 5, 7, 9][1,3,5,7,9] which is an arithmetic progression."
      }
    ]
